{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 hsuanice Library\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shared code used by hsuanice scripts such as RGWH and AudioSweet. Install this package together with any hsuanice script. It adds nothing to the Action List.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 AudioSweet ReaImGui\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Complete AudioSweet control center with ImGui interface for managing FX chains and presets.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Quick Start\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Help \u8594 ? User Manual: Full documentation with workflows and tips\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Help \u8594 ? About: Reference and credits\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Reference\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Inspired by AudioSuite-like Script by Tim Chimes 'AudioSweet' is a name originally given by Tim Chimes. This project continues to use the name in reference to his original work.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Original: Renders selected plugin to selected media item Written for REAPER 5.1 with Lua v1.1 12/22/2015 - Added PreventUIRefresh http://timchimes.com/scripting-with-reaper-audiosuite/\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Development\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script was developed with the assistance of AI tools including ChatGPT and Claude AI.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ImGui-based GUI for configuring and running RGWH Core operations. Provides visual controls for all RGWH Wrapper Template parameters.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 hsuanice Scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER scripts for audio post-production, by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Install {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER: {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories...} and paste:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/hsuanice/ReaScripts/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages}, search for {\f1 hsuanice}, and install:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b hsuanice Library} (required by every script below)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b RGWH} and/or {\b AudioSweet}\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ReaImGui} \u8212- install with ReaPack ({\i ReaTeam Extensions} repository, included by default).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b SWS Extension} \u8212- optional; a few features use it (e.g. {\i Retain Glue Cues}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b BWF MetaEdit} ({\f1 bwfmetaedit} command-line tool) \u8212- optional; only needed for timecode (BWF TimeReference) embedding.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Moving from hsuanice/PublicBeta\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository replaces {\f1 hsuanice/PublicBeta}, which is no longer updated. Both install to the same folder, so remove PublicBeta first:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Manage repositories}, right-click {\b hsuanice Scripts} (PublicBeta) > {\b Uninstall}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Import this repository and install the packages as above.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | Category | What it does | |---|---|---| | RGWH | Rendering | Render or glue items with handles (GUI + Glue / Render shortcuts) | | AudioSweet | Rendering | AudioSuite-style workflow in REAPER, Pro Tools style (GUI + Run / Preview / Solo shortcuts, FX Alias tools) | | hsuanice Library | Library | Shared code used by the scripts above; adds nothing to the Action List |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Release notes are shown in ReaPack. Older history is in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "Changelogs/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Changelogs/
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Credits\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The scripts in this repository are created and maintained by hsuanice, with the assistance of AI tools such as ChatGPT and Claude.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 AudioSweet is inspired by the AudioSuite-like script by Tim Chimes. "AudioSweet" is a name originally given by Tim Chimes; this project continues to use the name in reference to his original work. Original: "Renders selected plugin to selected media item", written for REAPER 5.1 with Lua (v1.1, 2015-12-22) \u8212- http://timchimes.com/scripting-with-reaper-audiosuite/\par}
}
